've traveled over  from germany  we understand that they have been  abiding by all of the government  regulations when it comes to  isolating because of covid but they are  of course allowed to attend  uh the funeral on the weekend but yeah  it is very much  a family affair of course in any other  time any other year you would have  expected  hundreds of people to attend the funeral  of the duke of edinburgh but because of  covid  that very small 30 congregation  all of whom will fit inside and the  choir that very intimate space  inside saint george's chapel and we're  told that any members of staff who are  anywhere near the chapel they're simply  there to make sure that  proceedings run as they should we're  also given a few more details  about the funeral procession and also  the service  um as well so we know that it's going to  be the prince of wales and princess anne  who will  lead some of that procession of other  members of the family  of course also prince william prince  harry are going to be involved between  them however as they're walking will be  their cousin peter phillips also we now  know that the queen will travel by car  behind the coffin she'll be in that car  with  a lady in waiting also as other people  who are carrying out funerals at the  moment  there will be social distancing in place  also  all the congregation will wear face  masks and they will not  sing um but also we've been getting more  details about  the ways that prince philip um has been  involved in in shaping his own funeral  and some new pictures have been released  of that rather  unique vehicle which will carry his  coffin during that procession  so this land rover that he helped to  design which i think is  a lovely touch for a man that we've  often spoken about this week haven't we  about how  modern and radical he could be at times  so yeah a few more details about the  funeral which will take place  on saturday but of course we keep being  reminded this is a very important family  occasion this is still a family uh in  mourning at the moment but hugely  appreciative of all the messages they've  had  from across the uk and around the world  remembering a man that meant so much to  them  yeah and a lot of speculation rhiannon  obviously about his  german relatives and as you say there  are  i'm just seeing a three i think there  which is uh which is interesting of  itself  it is but i think a lot of people will  reflect back on on the time when  um prince philip married um princess  elizabeth and actually at the time his  german relatives weren't  welcome to that wedding it was so soon  after the second world war  and some of his sisters of course um  held spouses who had nazi links so  there was this suspicion about them  understandably and so they weren't  invited to the wedding but i think  um over the years we have seen the queen  and the duke make visits to germany  and yeah i think it is that that  reflection of this being a family affair  of course we're so used to talking about  those senior royals here in the uk but  i think really lovely to see that some  of um prince phillips side the family  have also been invited but we kept being  reminded today just how involved  prince philip had been in the planning  but ultimately it's the queen who has  had to  to sign off these final plans and also i  think one thing that is worth mentioning  um is that none of the family are going  to wear military uniform  and that in itself is interesting of  course there is going to be an enormous  military presence um certainly inside  the castle grounds here at windsor we  keep being reminded that all of that  ceremony is going to take place  away from from the public inside the  castle grounds  but interestingly that the family are  not wearing military uniforms you would  of course expect that usually with  with a big ceremonial funeral like this  but i think the queen and others within  the family have decided that  it's best that they wear morning dress  with medals  i think to make sure there isn't too  much attention on  as you could describe it recent family  differences  and those within the family who have  stepped away from royal duties  and had to step away from their military  titles i think for the family  the attention very much has to be on the  duke of edinburgh  and they do not want too much discussion  about problems that have happened within  the family  certainly over the last year a year or  so  absolutely rhiannon thank you very much  indeed
 

